  "intentionalDifferences": [
    "One asset lifecycle serves all typed facades; adapters do not own retries, polling, or hooks.",
    "Submission retries default to zero; a positive count requires the corresponding explicit model idempotency capability. Status retries default to two.",
    "Operation envelopes bind provider, model, kind, and specification version and validate their JSON payload.",
    "URL assets remain references and are not downloaded implicitly.",
    "Active public-call timeout and completion-wait timeout are separate; completion waiting includes the final status request after a webhook. Terminal error/abort cleanup hooks are still awaited after cancellation.",
    "Lifecycle hooks are awaited and their errors propagate without changing an already selected terminal outcome.",
    "Cancellation is an explicit provider operation; aborting local waiting is not remote cancellation.",
    "Custom poll.delay replaces sleeping only and does not make the executor durable."
  ]
